From 8c327e8f0f2c62fb33ea7cb3117e569495529783 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 03:09:17 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] 958: six independent prompt reads run together instead of one
 after another

Live timings (12 Oct, 402 runs since 18:56Z): the model is called at
2.3 s median (p90 3.5 s, max 5.7 s) after the owner's message. The
server's own-answers chain that d59e722 would skip costs ~0 (max 0.4 s).
The cost is the prompt build after the parallel reads: median 1.0 s,
p90 2.1 s, max 3.8 s. Six awaits there ran in sequence: held asks, ask
states, wave note, first ask, the day's contact question, the
no-phonebook note.

They don't depend on each other, so they now run in one Promise.all. Only
the daily question writes, and only to its own table, which none of the
others read. The monthly contacts reminder still runs after the day's
question it gives way to. The prompt text and its order are unchanged.
Two source-wiring tests follow the new shape.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
